<title>USA: Banco Santiago files for $200 mln in notes.</title>
<headline>Banco Santiago files for $200 mln in notes.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banco Santiago, Chile's largest bank, filed Friday with the U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission to offer up to $200 million in subordinated notes.</p>
<p>Underwriters for the offering are: UBS Securities, Salomon Brothers Inc, HSBC James Capel and Banco Central Hispanoamericano.</p>
<p>Proceeds from the sale will be used to increase Santiago's regulatory capital base and for other general corporate purposes.</p>
</text>
